Here are the official Kakilima project rules written as clear, strict sentences that any developer or AI must follow at all times:

1. Every new feature must be placed inside `/lib/features/` and must contain exactly three folders: `data/`, `domain/`, and `presentation/`.  
2. No Supabase query is ever allowed outside of a file located in `features/.../data/datasources/`.  
3. All UI screens must extend `GetView<SomeController>` and must never call `Get.find()` inside the build method.  
4. Every feature must have its own Binding class that registers its controller(s) and use cases using `Get.lazyPut()`.  
5. All asynchronous operations must return `Either<Failure, T>` from the domain layer using the `dartz` package.  
6. Vendor location must be updated to Supabase every 5 minutes (±30 seconds) using Workmanager, even when the app is killed.  
7. Background location permission (`ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION`) and foreground service permission must be requested on Android immediately after a vendor logs in.  
8. A vendor is automatically marked inactive if `last_seen_at` is older than 20 minutes; this logic is enforced by a Supabase trigger, not in the app.  
9. Only one stall is allowed per vendor; attempting to create a second stall must be blocked.  
10. The discover map must only show stalls where `is_active = true` and within 3 km of the user using PostGIS `st_dwithin`.  
11. All images must be displayed using `CachedNetworkImage` with a placeholder and error widget.  
12. No Hive, no offline caching, and no image upload features are allowed in v1.  
13. No reviews, favorites, AI location suggestions, or analytics screens are permitted in v1.  
14. All streams opened from Supabase must be canceled inside the controller’s `onClose()` method.  
15. No `setState()`, `Bloc`, `Provider`, or `Riverpod` is ever allowed — only GetX with `.obs` is permitted.  
16. All location requests must use `LocationAccuracy.high` and must respect Android 11+ background location rules.  
17. VendorLocationService.start() must be called exactly once immediately after successful vendor login and never again.  
18. Hard-coded search radius is 3 km; no user-configurable radius in v1.  
19. Stall names can have an enhanced AI version, but the original name must always be stored separately.  
20. Any deviation from these rules must be explicitly approved in writing by the lead developer before committing code.

These 20 sentences are the law of the project. Follow them exactly, no exceptions.